-- title:
--   Pairwise coprime odd numbers in short windows
-- statement:
--   Let $d, X, H \in \mathbb N$ and let $A_0, \dots, A_{d-1}$ be natural numbers with $A_i + H \le X$. If $H$ exceeds the explicit sieve bound $\mathrm{sieveBound}(d, X)$, then one can choose odd numbers $s_i$ with $A_i < s_i \le A_i + H$ that are pairwise coprime:
--
--   $$\exists s,\ \big(\forall i,\ s_i \text{ odd},\ A_i < s_i \le A_i + H\big) \wedge \big(\forall i \ne j,\ \gcd(s_i, s_j) = 1\big).$$
--
--   The numbers $s_i$ serve as pairwise coprime moduli for the CRT steps of the round-six stack; the proof is a Brun pure sieve combined with a greedy choice.
--
--   In Lean:
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem J6Sieve.exists_coprime_in_windows (d X H : ℕ) (A : Fin d → ℕ) (hA : ∀ i, A i + H ≤ X)
--       (hH : sieveBound d X < H) :
--       ∃ s : Fin d → ℕ, (∀ i, Odd (s i) ∧ A i < s i ∧ s i ≤ A i + H) ∧
--         Pairwise (fun i j => Nat.Coprime (s i) (s j))
--   ```
